{"gbl_mdVersion_s":"Aardvark","id":"harvard-ghgis1867northgermanfed","dct_title_s":"Germany : North German Federation Boundary Lines, 1867, German Historical GIS","gbl_wxsIdentifier_s":"vector_public:GHGIS1867NORTHGERMANFED","dct_accessRights_s":"Public","dcat_bbox":"ENVELOPE(4.819391, 23.157687, 56.025202, 47.401637)","dct_creator_sm":["HGIS Germany (Andreas Kunz, Leonhard Dietze)","IEG-Maps / Berlin Data Pool (Andreas Kunz, Robert Moeschl)","Institut fur Europaische Geschichte (Mainz, Rhineland-Palatinate, Germany)","Fachhochschule Mainz (Mainz, Rhineland-Palatinate, Germany)"],"dct_issued_s":"2007","dct_description_sm":["These lines represent the boundary of the North German Federation (Norddeutscher Bund) in 1867. This Federation included Prussia and the northern German states as well as the territory of Hohenzollern in the south. It excluded the south German states (Bavaria, Wurttemberg, Baden). One state - Hesse-Darmstadt - was within the Federation only by membership of its northern territorial domain."],"dct_format_s":"Shapefile","locn_geometry":"ENVELOPE(4.819391, 23.157687, 56.025202, 47.401637)","gbl_indexYear_im":[1867],"gbl_mdModified_dt":"2011-08-08T00:00:00Z","schema_provider_s":"Harvard","dct_publisher_sm":["HGIS Germany"],"dct_spatial_sm":["Germany","German Confederation","Central Europe","Germany","Belgium","Czech Republic","Denmark","Lithuania","Kaliningrad Oblast","Poland"],"dct_subject_sm":["Political Divisions","sovereign states","boundaries","Boundaries","Administrative and political divisions","German states"],"dct_temporal_sm":["1867"],"harvard_collectionID_sm":["990126902100203941"],"dct_identifier_sm":["https://hgl.harvard.edu/catalog/harvard-ghgis1867northgermanfed","GHGIS1867NORTHGERMANFED","https://id.lib.harvard.edu/alma/990126902100203941/catalog"],"gbl_resourceClass_sm":["Datasets"],"dct_references_s":"{\"http://www.opengis.net/cat/csw/csdgm\":\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/harvard-library/harvard-geodata/main/fgdc/GHGIS1867NORT